        "language": "en",
        "bound_author_id": 2545,
        "text": "Eric Evans shows how teams can design software around the business problems it needs to solve. He describes how developers and domain experts build a shared vocabulary and express their understanding in the code. With examples, he introduces entities, value objects and aggregates, then turns to the boundaries between models in larger systems. The book also explains how teams can refine a design as their understanding of the domain changes.",
